Original commit body from ca2fd22ef85c468d99787bf16c6069acb0964b7f:

`resources` hardcoded seven routes (no `PUT /:id -> :update`) and read the
third argument only when it was an atom, so `only:`/`except:` were ignored.
It now mirrors Phoenix.Router.Resource: the action set
[index, edit, new, show, create, update, delete] filtered by only:/except:,
`update` on both PATCH and PUT, `singleton: true` (no index, no /:id) and
`param:`; options are read in bare keyword and bracketed-list form, and a
non-literal option falls back to the full set.

Route macros never applied the enclosing `scope` alias, so
`scope "/", AppWeb do get "/", PageController, :home end` pointed at
`PageController`. A scope-aware walk now carries the alias (positional or
`alias:`, lexically expanded, nested scopes concatenated, `alias: false`
resets) and every get/post/.../live/resources controller is expanded and
prefixed, as Phoenix does. On thc all 377 router markers are now fully
qualified (were 2) and every dispatches_to edge lands on the named module.

The scope PATH prefix (WI-kibij) is not part of this change.

